<section id="english" lang="en">
<h1>DrumPads Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="date">Last updated: November 1, 2026</p>
<p>This policy explains how BeHonor Studio, the developer of DrumPads (“we”) handles information in the Android app DrumPads (package: <code>com.behonor.drumpads</code>). For privacy questions and requests, contact <a href="mailto:beehonorstu@gmail.com">beehonorstu@gmail.com</a>.</p>
<h2>1. Music and information on your device</h2>
<p>DrumPads lets you play drum pads, create beats, import backing audio, record pad performances, and export or share projects and audio. Projects, pad-performance recordings, preferences, imported-file references, and the expiration time of rewarded kit access are stored on your device. Recording a pad performance captures the app’s musical events; the app does not request microphone permission.</p>
<p>The current version uses bundled music resources and audio you select through Android’s document picker. It does not upload your projects, recordings, or imported audio to a developer-operated server. When you export or share, the files are sent to the app or destination you choose; that service’s privacy policy also applies. Android backup or device-transfer services may back up or restore app data according to your device settings and their own policies. Clearing app data does not delete copies you previously exported, shared, or backed up.</p>
<h2>2. Google advertising and privacy messages</h2>
<p>We use Google AdMob through the Google Mobile Ads (GMA Next-Gen) SDK and Google’s User Messaging Platform (UMP). UMP requests privacy information and presents consent or opt-out forms where applicable. The app checks whether UMP permits ad requests before initializing the advertising SDK and requesting ads.</p>
<p>Google’s advertising SDK may automatically collect and share:</p>
<ul>
<li>IP address, which may be used to estimate your approximate location;</li>
<li>app and advertisement interactions, such as app launches, taps, and video views;</li>
<li>diagnostic and performance information, such as launch time, hangs, and energy usage;</li>
<li>device and account identifiers, including Android advertising ID, app set ID, and other account-related identifiers where applicable.</li>
</ul>
<p>Google and its advertising partners use this information for advertising, analytics, and fraud prevention. Ad personalization depends on your choices, applicable requirements, and Google’s ad-serving controls. Non-personalized or limited ads may still process data for delivery, measurement, security, or fraud prevention. SDK data is encrypted in transit using TLS. Privacy messaging also processes and stores the choices and signals needed to apply your privacy preferences.</p>
<p>Learn more: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>, <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">How Google uses information from apps that use its services</a>, and <a href="https://developers.google.com/admob/android/next-gen/privacy/play-data-disclosure">GMA Next-Gen data disclosure</a>.</p>
<h2>3. Optional rewarded ads and 24-hour access</h2>
<p>Jazz is available without watching an advertisement. You can choose to watch a rewarded ad to unlock all four other drum kits for 24 hours. Access is granted after the advertising SDK reports an earned reward. The app stores the access expiration time locally. Cancelling the confirmation, an unavailable advertisement, or an advertisement error does not itself grant a reward.</p>
<p>Ads may be requested and prepared after privacy requirements are resolved, before you choose to watch one. Choosing not to watch an ad does not necessarily prevent every SDK-related network request. Rewarded playback starts only after you choose to watch. Consent to personalized advertising and choosing to watch an ad are separate choices.</p>
<h2>4. Your privacy choices</h2>
<p>Where required by UMP, the app’s Settings page provides “Ad privacy choices” to review or change your choices, including withdrawing consent or opting out where offered. You can also reset or delete the advertising ID through Android settings where supported. These controls do not necessarily stop all advertising data processing. Jazz and the app’s local music functions remain available when ads cannot be shown.</p>
<h2>5. Retention, deletion, and requests</h2><p>If you contact support, we receive your email address and the information you choose to send, and use them to respond and resolve your request. We retain support correspondence as needed for support and legitimate recordkeeping, or as required by law. Please avoid sending unnecessary personal information.</p>
<p>You can delete local works using the app’s available controls, remove imported audio references, or clear the app’s storage/uninstall it to remove data in its private storage. Back up any works you want to keep first. Original imported files and exported or shared copies must be deleted at their respective locations. Google and other services you choose retain data according to their own policies; clearing DrumPads storage does not delete their records.</p>
<p>Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or restrict the processing of personal data, or to object, withdraw consent, opt out, or complain to a supervisory authority. Contact the email above for requests concerning information we hold. For information held by Google, use Google’s privacy controls and request channels. DrumPads does not require an in-app account.</p>
<h2>6. Children</h2>
<p>We do not knowingly collect children’s personal information through a developer-operated account or server. If you believe a child has provided personal information in connection with DrumPads, contact us. Advertising services have their own data practices described above.</p>
<h2>7. Security and international processing</h2>
<p>We use Android’s app storage and permission mechanisms for local data. No storage or transmission method guarantees absolute security. Google may process advertising and consent information in countries other than yours under its privacy policies and applicable safeguards.</p>
<h2>8. Changes and contact</h2>
<p>We may update this policy as the app or its services change. The date above indicates the latest revision. Privacy contact: <a href="mailto:beehonorstu@gmail.com">beehonorstu@gmail.com</a>.</p>
</section>
<section id="chinese" lang="zh-CN">
<h1>DrumPads 隐私政策</h1>
<p class="date">更新日期：2026 年 11 月 1 日</p>
<p>本政策说明 BeHonor Studio（DrumPads 开发者，以下简称“我们”）如何在 Android 应用 DrumPads（包名：<code>com.behonor.drumpads</code>）中处理信息。隐私问题与相关请求请联系：<a href="mailto:beehonorstu@gmail.com">beehonorstu@gmail.com</a>。</p>
<h2>1. 本机音乐与数据</h2>
<p>DrumPads 支持鼓垫演奏、节奏创作、导入伴奏、记录鼓垫演奏，以及导出或分享工程和音频。作品、演奏录制、偏好设置、导入文件引用和激励解锁到期时间保存在设备上。录制演奏记录的是应用内音乐事件，应用不申请麦克风权限。</p>
<p>当前版本使用内置音乐资源和你通过 Android 文件选择器选取的音频，不会把工程、演奏录制或导入音频上传到开发者运营的服务器。主动导出或分享时，文件会交给你选择的应用或目标位置，相关服务的隐私政策同时适用。Android 系统备份或设备迁移服务可能根据设备设置及其自身政策备份或恢复应用数据。清除应用数据不会删除已经导出、分享或备份的副本。</p>
<h2>2. Google 广告与隐私消息</h2>
<p>我们通过 Google Mobile Ads（GMA Next-Gen）SDK 使用 Google AdMob，并使用 Google User Messaging Platform（UMP）获取隐私状态，在适用情况下展示同意或退出选项。应用在初始化广告 SDK、请求广告之前，先检查 UMP 是否允许请求广告。</p>
<p>Google 广告 SDK 可能自动收集并共享以下数据：</p>
<ul>
<li>IP 地址，可用于推算设备的大致位置；</li>
<li>应用与广告互动，例如应用启动、点击和视频观看；</li>
<li>诊断和性能信息，例如启动时间、卡顿和能耗；</li>
<li>设备与账号标识符，包括 Android 广告 ID、应用集 ID，以及适用情况下与设备已登录账号有关的其他标识符。</li>
</ul>
<p>Google 及其广告合作伙伴将这些信息用于广告、分析和防范欺诈。是否提供个性化广告取决于你的选择、适用要求及 Google 广告投放设置。非个性化或受限广告仍可能为投放、衡量、安全或防范欺诈处理数据。SDK 数据通过 TLS 加密传输。隐私消息服务还会处理和保存执行隐私偏好所需的选择及信号。</p>
<p>详情请参阅：<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy?hl=zh-CN">Google 隐私政策</a>、<a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites?hl=zh-CN">Google 如何使用来自使用其服务的应用的信息</a>、<a href="https://developers.google.com/admob/android/next-gen/privacy/play-data-disclosure">GMA Next-Gen 数据披露说明</a>。</p>
<h2>3. 可选激励广告与 24 小时解锁</h2>
<p>Jazz 鼓组无需观看广告即可使用。你可主动观看一条激励广告，解锁另外全部四套鼓组 24 小时。应用仅在广告 SDK 返回已获得奖励的回调后发放权益，并在本地保存到期时间。取消确认、广告不可用或广告报错本身不会发放奖励。</p>
<p>隐私要求处理完成后，应用可能在你选择观看前请求和预加载广告，因此不观看广告并不代表完全不会产生 SDK 网络请求。只有你主动选择观看后才会播放激励广告。是否同意个性化广告与是否选择观看广告是两个独立选择。</p>
<h2>4. 隐私选择</h2>
<p>当 UMP 要求提供入口时，应用设置页会显示“广告隐私选项”，以便查看或修改选择，包括界面提供的撤回同意或退出选项。你也可在支持的 Android 系统设置中重置或删除广告 ID。这些控制不一定停止所有广告数据处理。广告无法展示时，Jazz 和本地音乐功能仍然可用。</p>
<h2>5. 保存、删除与权利请求</h2><p>联系支持时，我们会收到你的邮箱地址及你主动发送的信息，用于回复和处理请求。支持通信会在提供支持、合理留存记录或法律要求所需期间保存。请避免发送不必要的个人信息。</p>
<p>你可以使用应用提供的操作删除本地作品、移除导入音频引用，或通过清除应用存储、卸载应用删除私有目录中的数据。请先备份需要保留的作品。原始导入文件、导出或分享的副本需要在各自位置删除。Google 及你选择的其他服务按照各自政策保存数据；清除 DrumPads 存储不会删除这些服务的记录。</p>
<p>根据所在地要求，你可能享有访问、更正、删除、限制处理、反对处理、撤回同意、退出或向监管机构投诉等权利。对于我们持有的信息，请通过上述邮箱提出请求。对于 Google 持有的信息，请使用 Google 的隐私控制与请求渠道。DrumPads 不要求注册应用内账号。</p>
<h2>6. 儿童信息</h2>
<p>我们不会通过开发者运营的账号或服务器有意收集儿童个人信息。如果你认为儿童在使用 DrumPads 过程中提供了个人信息，请联系我们。广告服务的数据处理方式见上文。</p>
<h2>7. 安全与跨境处理</h2>
<p>我们使用 Android 的应用存储与权限机制处理本地数据，但任何存储或传输方式都无法保证绝对安全。Google 可能依据其隐私政策和适用保障措施，在你所在国家或地区之外处理广告及同意信息。</p>
<h2>8. 更新与联系</h2>
<p>应用或服务变化时，我们可能更新本政策，页面上方日期表示最近修订时间。隐私联系邮箱：<a href="mailto:beehonorstu@gmail.com">beehonorstu@gmail.com</a>。</p>
</section>

